def solve(s):
    parts = s.split('.')
    if len(parts) != 4:
        return False
    for p in parts:
        if not p.isdigit():
            return False
        if len(p) > 1 and p[0] == '0':
            return False
        if int(p) > 255:
            return False
    return True

Note: isdigit() could accept unicode digits like '١٢٣' (Arabic digits) — int() would parse them too. Hidden tests might include weird cases. Safer: check all(c in '0123456789' for c in p) and p non-empty. Also '²' (superscript) is isdigit() True but int() fails — so avoid isdigit.

